                                                "sense_id": "0cf6922d-3db5-3af0-a4f4-ecf87461c2fd",
                                                "text": "The theory of p'''-adic analytic functions in domains other than simple disks is not very well known yet, although such kind of functions happens to intervene in questions linked to p'''-adic functional analysis, number theory, and others."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5f2096a-5501-48c9-870d-83a8592701ba",
                                                "sense_id": "0cf6922d-3db5-3af0-a4f4-ecf87461c2fd",
                                                "text": "1997, Fernando Q. Gouvêa, p-adic Numbers: An Introduction, Springer, 2nd Edition, page 60,\nDefinition 3.3.3 The ring of p'''-adic integers is the valuation ring\nZ ₚ=x∈ Q ₚ:|x|ₚ<1."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "951cc3f0-1d9a-4ec1-89a3-4951df7ab557",
                                                "sense_id": "0cf6922d-3db5-3af0-a4f4-ecf87461c2fd",
                                                "text": "2. Preliminaries\n3. A p'''-adic Cauchy problem\n4. The p'''-adic Hilbert transform\n5. The boundaries in the p'''-adic space L^q\n[…]"
